&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quadlet makes use of systemd to manage your containers for you&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;It does most of the supporting work too: volumes, networks, image builds, and referencing secrets!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Secure enough for my small scale, using rootless containers
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rootless with Quadlet + Podman is an easy as &lt;code&gt;systemctl --user start&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stable enough to survive restarts &amp;amp; neglect
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;systemd&lt;/code&gt; handles all my restart woes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Podman&#39;s &lt;code&gt;AutoUpdate=registry&lt;/code&gt; ensure my images are up to date&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;(Bonus) Dual-stack IPv4 &amp;amp; v6.
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;It was just a flag in the &lt;code&gt;.network&lt;/code&gt;, how easy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Overall, this has been a setup &amp;amp; forget situation.
The only time I have had an issue is when the container builds broke
due dependencies moving between major version of &lt;code&gt;libdns&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I&#39;d give it a 4/5, good for home-scale 👍&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
